🌟 Full Stack Developer Learning Guide (Till 30th December)
🎯 Goal

Become proficient in Full Stack Development with Java (Spring Boot) for backend, React for frontend, and deployment-ready skills using DevOps tools (Git, Jenkins, AWS, Docker, etc.).

🗓️ PHASE 1: Backend Foundation (Nov 14 – Nov 30)
🔹 Topics:

1. Core Java (Fundamentals + Advanced)

OOP Concepts: Class, Object, Inheritance, Polymorphism, Abstraction, Encapsulation

Exception Handling

Collections Framework (List, Set, Map, Queue)

Streams & Lambda Expressions

File Handling

Java 8+ Features (Functional Interfaces, Optional, Streams API)

2. Spring Boot (Beginner to Intermediate)

Spring Boot Basics, Annotations, Layers (Controller, Service, Repository)

REST API creation

Validation, Exception Handling

Using Lombok, SLF4J Logging

Connecting Spring Boot with MySQL using Spring Data JPA

CRUD Operations with Repository Layer

3. Hibernate (JPA Basics)

ORM Concepts

Entity, Table Mapping, One-to-Many, Many-to-Many relationships

Lazy vs Eager Loading

JPQL / Criteria Queries

🗓️ PHASE 2: Advanced Backend + Microservices (Dec 1 – Dec 10)
🔹 Topics:

1. Microservices Architecture

Monolithic vs Microservices

Service Registry (Eureka), API Gateway

Feign Client for inter-service communication

Config Server, Load Balancing (Ribbon/Spring Cloud LoadBalancer)

2. Security

JWT Authentication (User Login, Token Validation)

OAuth2 Overview

Spring Security Integration

3. Build Tools

Maven & Gradle – structure, dependencies, plugins, build lifecycle

🗓️ PHASE 3: Frontend (React.js) (Dec 11 – Dec 17)
🔹 Topics:

1. React Basics

JSX, Components, Props, State

Event Handling, Forms

Lifecycle & Hooks (useState, useEffect, useContext)

Routing with React Router

Fetching REST API data from Spring Boot

2. Styling

CSS, TailwindCSS / Bootstrap

Component-based UI design

3. Integration

Connecting React with Spring Boot REST APIs

Displaying data from MySQL through backend

🗓️ PHASE 4: Database & DevOps (Dec 18 – Dec 23)
🔹 Topics:

1. MySQL

DDL, DML, Joins, Aggregate Functions

Normalization & Indexing

Writing Queries for CRUD operations

Integrating MySQL with Spring Boot

2. Version Control

Git Basics: init, add, commit, push, pull, branch, merge

GitHub / GitLab / Bitbucket workflow

Creating a repository and pushing project code

3. CI/CD

Jenkins setup

GitHub Actions / GitLab CI/CD pipelines

Build → Test → Deploy automation

🗓️ PHASE 5: Cloud, Containers, and Monitoring (Dec 24 – Dec 28)
🔹 Topics:

1. AWS

EC2 (Deploying Spring Boot & React app)

S3 for file storage

RDS for MySQL

2. Docker

Creating Dockerfile

Building & running containers for Spring Boot + React

Docker Compose

3. Monitoring & Logging

Using SLF4J + Logback

Application logs in AWS CloudWatch

Basic Monitoring Setup

🗓️ PHASE 6: Final Project & Deployment (Dec 29 – Dec 30)
🔹 Activities:

✅ End-to-End Full Stack Project

Project Idea: Employee Management System / Online Game / Insurance Calculator / E-Commerce

SRS/BRS Documentation

Spring Boot REST APIs

React.js Frontend

MySQL Database

Secure APIs with JWT

CI/CD with Jenkins or GitHub Actions

Dockerize & Deploy to AWS EC2

✅ Testing

Unit Testing with JUnit + Mockito

Integration Testing using Postman

✅ Deliverables

Live deployed project link

GitHub repository

Documentation (README + SRS + API Docs)

📘 Suggested Weekly Plan Summary

| Week   | Duration        | Focus Area                              |
| ------ | --------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Week 1 | Nov 14 – Nov 20 | Core Java + OOP + Collections + Streams |
| Week 2 | Nov 21 – Nov 30 | Spring Boot + JPA + Hibernate           |
| Week 3 | Dec 1 – Dec 10  | Microservices + Security + Maven        |
| Week 4 | Dec 11 – Dec 17 | React.js Frontend Development           |
| Week 5 | Dec 18 – Dec 23 | MySQL + Git/GitHub + CI/CD              |
| Week 6 | Dec 24 – Dec 28 | AWS + Docker + Monitoring               |
| Week 7 | Dec 29 – Dec 30 | Final Project + Testing + Deployment    |
